# EXAMPLE ONLY: a CODEOWNERS for the shared configs repository, one block per
# facility. Copy it into the configs repo as .github/CODEOWNERS and replace
# every <placeholder> with the org's own teams and folder names; nothing here
# names a real team, experiment or facility.
#
# One configs repo serves several facilities, each with its own services box
# (GeecsConfigurator/DEPLOYMENT.md). A box commits only under the experiments
# and analysis folders its site.env names; a human change goes by pull
# request, and this file routes each pull request to the facility whose
# folders it touches. It binds only when the main ruleset turns on "Require
# review from Code Owners". The GitHub App is on the bypass list, so its
# commits (the operator tier, from the box that owns the folder) are not
# reviewed here: ownership is enforced on the box, and the `validate` check
# names an invalid commit on GitHub either way.
#
# The last matching line wins: the catch-all first, the facilities after.

# Everything not claimed below (the README, the logbook templates, a new
# experiment before it has an owner): the configs repo's maintainers.
*                                               @<org>/<configs-maintainers>

# Facility A: its experiments, and its folders in the shared analysis tree.
/scanner_configs/experiments/<ExperimentA1>/    @<org>/<facility-a-maintainers>
/scanner_configs/experiments/<ExperimentA2>/    @<org>/<facility-a-maintainers>
/scan_analysis_configs/analyzers/<FacilityA>/   @<org>/<facility-a-maintainers>
/scan_analysis_configs/groups/<FacilityA>/      @<org>/<facility-a-maintainers>

# Facility B: the same shape.
/scanner_configs/experiments/<ExperimentB1>/    @<org>/<facility-b-maintainers>
/scan_analysis_configs/analyzers/<FacilityB>/   @<org>/<facility-b-maintainers>
/scan_analysis_configs/groups/<FacilityB>/      @<org>/<facility-b-maintainers>

# The check itself and this file: the configs repo's maintainers alone.
/.github/                                       @<org>/<configs-maintainers>
